v1=("Model-independent integral of the Xb55 (8.6x6.0\") CH3OH J_-1-J_0 E J=1-3 blend (163.52 GHz observed, spw22, beam-aperture spectra, +-400 km/s about the region centre) depends strongly on the baseline because the spectrum has a red wing and a negative ramp toward the spw edge (v>3000 km/s). "
 f"Jy/beam km/s for baselines (const from blue side / const all-free / linear / linear narrow / quadratic): N {tab('N')} | S {tab('S')} | Bridge {tab('Bridge')} | W {tab('W')}. "
 f"Adopted (median of 10 baseline x window choices, 16-84% range): N {T['N']['Iblend']:.2f}, S {T['S']['Iblend']:.2f} ({T['S']['blend_range'][0]:.2f}-{T['S']['blend_range'][1]:.2f} full range), Bridge {T['Bridge']['Iblend']:.2f} ({T['Bridge']['blend_range'][0]:.2f}-{T['Bridge']['blend_range'][1]:.2f}), W {H['W']['Iblend']:.2f}; statistical error only +-0.1-0.15. "
 "So the earlier '+-30% template systematic' is too small: the baseline choice moves the blend by a factor ~2-4 (N 0.5-2.0). team-a p0001's 2.23 (N; Gaussian + linear baseline) and the reviewer's 1.84 sit at the linear-baseline end; our earlier 0.97 (N) / 1.38 (S) (HCO+ template, median baseline) is mid-range; all are within the baseline-systematic range, and the claim 'agree within 20-30%' is not a measurement of the systematic. The line is real (peak 8-12 mJy/beam vs rms 2.1-2.3 per 1.95 MHz channel, 4-6 sigma per channel at S, Bridge, N; W 4 sigma), absent in E1, E2, Sblue (spectra: out/q9/s120a_spectra.png).")
