v2=(f"Optically thin LTE from W(254.015 2(0)-1(-1)E, Eu 20.1 K, log A -4.72)/W(blend) (K km/s; 254 line from Xb4f smoothed to the Xb55 beam, s21: S {T['S']['I254']:.2f}+-{T['S']['eI254']:.2f}, Bridge {T['Bridge']['I254']:.2f}+-{T['Bridge']['eI254']:.2f}, N {T['N']['I254']:.2f}+-{T['N']['eI254']:.2f} Jy/beam km/s) with the blend baseline range propagated by Monte Carlo (20000 draws): "
 f"S R_K={T['S']['R_K']:.2f} (16-84% {T['S']['R_K_16_84'][0]:.2f}-{T['S']['R_K_16_84'][1]:.2f}) -> Trot={tr('S')[1]:.0f} K (+{tr('S')[2]-tr('S')[1]:.0f}/-{tr('S')[1]-tr('S')[0]:.0f}); Bridge R_K={T['Bridge']['R_K']:.2f} -> Trot={tr('Bridge')[1]:.0f} K (16-84%: {tr('Bridge')[0]:.0f}->60+ K, i.e. only Trot>~7 K); N: 254 line not detected, Trot unconstrained (>12 K at 84%). "
 "So 'Trot~9 K' is reproduced as a central value at S (10 K) but is NOT a real constraint: 6-18 K allowed at S (1 sigma), >7 K at the Bridge. The earlier +-30% systematic gave 8-21 K (S), 9-44 K (Bridge): consistent, now with a larger honest range. LTE W254/Wblend: 4 K 0.79, 6 K 0.47, 8 K 0.35, 10 K 0.29, 15 K 0.22, 20 K 0.19, 30 K 0.16. J=4,5 (165.19, 165.37) 3-sigma limits (0.19-0.26, 0.17-0.18 Jy/beam km/s) allow T<~15-20 K only. Beam-averaged E-CH3OH column from the 254 line (9.4x6.3\" beam, thin, Q_E=0.5x0.235 T^1.5, no beam-filling correction): S N(E)~1.1e13 (T=10 K; 1.0-1.9e13 for 6-18 K), Bridge ~0.8e13 cm^-2 (A+E total x2); true column at 1\" scales larger if the emission is clumpy.")
