v3=("(1) Is the 'Q-branch excess' real? Not reproducible as excess. In the channel-space joint fit of the five Q lines (J=1-5) to the Xb55 spectra at N and S (s18, HCO+ template, 1.3x correlation-inflated rms), optically thin LTE at 8-10 K gives chi2=285 (N) / 303 (S) for ~400 channels (null 555 / 802): the blend + J=4,5 non-detections are consistent with a single cold Tex. The chi2=53/6 dof of p0001 comes from fitting integrated single-line windows: their own table (N, Xb55) has J=5 -0.37+-0.08 Jy/beam km/s (-4.4 sigma), J=7 -0.21+-0.09, J=6 -0.11+-0.08, J=4 -0.07+-0.12, i.e. negative amplitudes that no emission model fits, plus a blend of 2.23 at the high-baseline end of our range; both come from the linear baseline in +-450 km/s windows near the spw ramp. With the blend at its constant-baseline value (0.5-1.1) the 1.6x 'excess' disappears (factor 2 swing). Weak maser or unmodelled blend is not needed. Individual J=1,2,3 amplitudes are degenerate (overlap of 20 and 70 km/s vs 150 km/s width); only their sum is measured (our own s17 per-J chi2 19.8/28.9 for 3 dof has the same degeneracy; do not read it as an excess). "
 f"(2) Matched-beam contrast: region-integrated CH3OH blend/HCO+ 2-1 (K km/s, Xb55 aperture) = N {H['N']['ratioK']:.3f} ({H['N']['ratioK_16_84'][0]:.3f}-{H['N']['ratioK_16_84'][1]:.3f}), S {H['S']['ratioK']:.3f} ({H['S']['ratioK_16_84'][0]:.3f}-{H['S']['ratioK_16_84'][1]:.3f}), Bridge {H['Bridge']['ratioK']:.3f} ({H['Bridge']['ratioK_16_84'][0]:.3f}-{H['Bridge']['ratioK_16_84'][1]:.3f}), W {H['W']['ratioK']:.3f} ({H['W']['ratioK_16_84'][0]:.3f}-{H['W']['ratioK_16_84'][1]:.3f}): equal within errors at all four positions. At 9\" the beam contains N, S and the Bridge, so Xb55 cannot test N-vs-off-nuclear contrast; the 'off-nuclear enhancement' (0.04-0.07 Bridge/W vs N<0.022, S<0.03 at 1-4\") is a 1-4\" statement from the 254 line in Xb4d/Xb47-matched beams (p0016, report entries above) and rests on a single transition. The 254 line is recovered at the Bridge at the matched beam (Xb4d 0.46 vs Xb4f 0.60, ratio 0.77+-0.3), so the contrast is not a resolved-out artefact, but its size at the nuclei is limited by CH3OH being extended while HCO+ is compact: ratios taken at the HCO+ peaks are diluted. "
 "(3) Kinematics: CH3OH 254 centroid minus HCO+ 3-2 in the same pixel: S +16+-5, Bridge +10+-7 (Xb4f), +7+-2 (Xb4d Bridge), Sblue +43+-23 km/s (2 sigma): the CH3OH moves with the HCO+ at the systemic velocity, no outflow-velocity offset; NS 253.968 is excluded (-38..-47 km/s expected). Xb55 blend FWHM 142-153 km/s (three overlapping lines; intrinsic ~110-130 km/s) similar to HCO+. "
 "Net: the off-nuclear CH3OH is real as a line (4-6 sigma per channel in Xb55, 9.9 sigma matched filter at the Bridge in Xb4d, two transitions in two bands), cold (Trot ~10 K, 6-18 K at S; Bridge >7 K), extended on >1\" scales; the N/S non-detections and Bridge/W enhancement are single-transition and ~3-4 sigma, so medium confidence. p0001's unexplained Q-branch excess and chi2=53/6 are not confirmed: they trace the baseline choice, not excitation.")
R.append({'quantity':'Q9: net answer - is the off-nuclear (Bridge/W) CH3OH enhancement real, what is its excitation, and is the Q-branch excess real (check of team-a p0001)','target':'N, S, Bridge, W, Sblue (Xb55, Xb4f, Xb4d)','value':v3,
 'uncertainty':'Trot 6-18 K (S); blend integral factor 2-4 baseline systematic; ratios in value','unit':'ratios, K',
 'assumptions':[A('team-a numbers','/snapshots/team-a-s01/out/ch3oh_table.csv (Xb55 N: 2.23+-0.08; J=4-8 single-line windows)'),A('same beam','Xb55 ratios share the beam; Xb4f 254 line smoothed to the Xb55 beam with covariance-matched kernel (s21)')],
 'confidence':'medium','evidence':'out/q9/s120a_spectra.png, s120b-e json; out/s18_ch3oh_radex.txt; out/s20_254_centroids_*.json; out/s27_ch3oh_recovery.json'})
